/*
✒ Metadata
    - Title: Markdown Lint Rules (digiSpace Edition - v2.0)
    - File Name: .markdownlint.jsonc
    - Relative Path: .markdownlint.jsonc
    - Artifact Type: config
    - Version: 2.0.0
    - Date: 11/05/2026
    - Update: Thursday, November 05, 2026
    - Author: Dennis 'dendogg' Smaltz
    - A.I. Acknowledgement: Anthropic - Claude Opus 5.5
    - Signature: ︻デ═─── ✦ ✦ ✦ | Aim Twice, Shoot Once!

✒ Changelog:
    - 2.0.0 (11/05/2026) [dendogg + Anthropic - Claude Opus 5.5] — Created
      with the project documentation for the formal stack.

✒ Description:
    markdownlint settings for the project's documentation: the
    vscode-markdownlint defaults, except that table rows and code blocks
    may run past 80 characters.

✒ Key Features:
    - Prose wraps at 80 characters (MD013).
    - Table rows are exempt, so reference tables stay one row per item.
    - Code blocks are exempt, so commands are never broken.

✒ Other Important Information:
    - Dependencies: none; read by vscode-markdownlint and markdownlint-cli2
    - Compatible platforms: markdownlint 0.30+ in any editor or CI
---------
*/
{
  "default": true,
  "MD013": { "line_length": 80, "tables": false, "code_blocks": false }
}
